    {
      "id": "MILK",
      "label": "Milk",
      "notes": "Specific phrases come before the bare word they contain, because the first match wins and is the term shown as evidence: \"ice cream\" must precede \"cream\", and the qualified milks precede \"milk\". Cheeses are named individually: matching is by word token, so \"cheese\" cannot catch \"mozzarella\". The exclusions carry the plant-based analogues, which is what keeps bare \"milk\", \"cream\", \"butter\", \"curd\" and \"dairy\" safe to list as definite terms. \"mustard\" is excluded for the same reason as under EGGS: it is one edit away from \"custard\".",
