    {
      "id": "EGGS",
      "label": "Eggs",
      "notes": "\"custard\" is listed here as well as under MILK: it is both. The egg-prefixed phrases precede bare \"egg\" so the evidence quoted is the specific one. \"mustard\" is excluded because it is one edit away from \"custard\", which the fuzzy near-miss pass would otherwise read as a possible egg on every mustard label.",
      "terms": [
        "egg white", "egg yolk", "egg albumin", "egg lecithin", "dried egg", "egg", "albumin",
        "albumen", "ovalbumin", "ovomucoid", "ovomucin", "ovovitellin", "ovotransferrin",
