    {
      "id": "WHEAT",
      "label": "Wheat",
      "notes": "Bare \"flour\", \"starch\", \"bran\" and \"noodle\" are ambiguous, so every common non-wheat flour, starch, bran and noodle is listed as an exclusion to stop them firing; the list is maintained, not exhaustive, so add to it when a new one shows up. \"sans gluten\" is kept as a false-positive guard: \"gluten\" is an English term, and French negates before the noun so the trailing-\"free\" rule cannot catch it. Barley, rye and oats are absent by design - Canada declares them as gluten sources separately from wheat, and they would need an allergen of their own.",
